Production at release 3, deployed straight to release 6: a rename of 4,
a drop of 5 and a backfill of 6, all in one plan, and the rows land as
they would have release by release.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL, photo TEXT) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'Pea Soup', 'soup.jpg'), (2, 'Rye Bread', NULL);
PRAGMA user_version = 3;

== after
-- @release 6
-- @drop 4 column dish title
-- @from 4 column dish name = title
-- @drop 5 column dish photo
-- @from 6 column dish slug = lower(replace(title, ' ', '-'))
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name = title, slug = lower(replace(title, ' ', '-'))
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name", "slug") SELECT "id", (
    title
    ), (
    lower(replace(title, ' ', '-'))
    ) FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"
migrated from release 3

== query
SELECT id, name, slug FROM dish ORDER BY id

== rows
1 | Pea Soup | pea-soup
2 | Rye Bread | rye-bread
